{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:0.2", "PA_ja_19:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Sīlavagga (The Chapter on Virtue)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:0.4"], "en": "9. The Jātaka of the Begged Meal:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:1.1", "PA_ja_19:1.2"], "en": "“If one is released after having been bound, yet while being released one is still bound;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:1.3"], "en": "The wise are not liberated in this way;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:1.4"], "en": "for the fool, liberation is a bond.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_19:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the ninth Jātaka, the Story of the Begged-for Alms.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"}
